# oracle: a cg minimization in a box shrink-wrapped in y and periodic in x (examples/indent/in.indent.min, first
#   minimization). As native LAMMPS does (src/min.cpp energy_force and src/fix_minimize.cpp reset_coords at b332f28),
#   after a line-search trial that reneighbored, the start point of an atom the rebuild wrapped across x moves to its
#   new image; the engine's next trial put the atom back across the boundary and rebuilt again (two builds in one
#   iteration), so the shrink-wrapped box was fitted to other positions: ly and the pressure 3e-3 off from iteration 11.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-10
dimension       2
boundary        p s p
atom_style      atomic
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 5
lattice         hex 0.9
region          box block 0 20 0 10 -0.25 0.25
create_box      2 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            * 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
region          1 block INF INF INF 1.25 INF INF
group           lower region 1
group           mobile subtract all lower
set             group lower type 2
fix             2 lower setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
fix             5 all enforce2d
thermo          1
thermo_style    custom step pe press ly nbuild
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
minimize        1.0e-6 1.0e-6 20 1000
